open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T08:21:32Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-05T18:42:20Z","updated_at":"2026-10-07T17:12:29Z","closed_at":"2026-10-07T14:25:41Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.6.3 and v4.7.2\n- Not reproducible in v4.5.2\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.2.stable - Manjaro Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Sat, 05 Sep 2026 01:29:32 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 7700S (RADV NAVI33) - AMD Ryzen AI 9 HX 370 w/ Radeon 890M (24 threads) - 30.63 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nEnabling both \"refraction\" and \"proximity fade\" on a BaseMaterial3D results in a shader compilation error.  It looks like this is being caused by two snippets of shader code that are added in `scene/resources/material.cpp` (lines 1768-1829) which share a variable name, so there could be similar issues when enabling two other properties in a material.\n\nIn these screenshots, enabling **either** refraction or proximity fade works fine in the MRP:\n<img width=\"3393\" height=\"1859\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bc6d252a-818a-4bbf-a1dc-3568ad816acd\" />\n<img width=\"3393\" height=\"1859\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/55de0511-b2f9-41ba-b2a2-6be04c68ec97\" />\n\nHowever, enabling both causes the compilation error and the material doesn't display correctly:\n<img width=\"3393\" height=\"1859\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9025dc0c-4932-4772-9e14-4ff5e69f1a0d\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a new mesh and assign a BaseMaterial3D to it\n2. Enable \"refraction\" on the material\n3. Enable \"proximity fade\" on the material\n4. The compilation error should appear in the output window\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[RefractionProximityFadeTest.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/33071985/RefractionProximityFadeTest.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124195/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124195/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}